  "description": "Original constructed exercises for an upper-undergraduate to graduate bridge. Prerequisites: intermediate microeconomics and macroeconomics, single-variable calculus, constrained optimization, elementary probability and conditional expectations, basic bank accounting, and introductory econometrics including instrumental variables. Graduate extensions use simple present-value sums, normal updating, and matrix rank. Official university materials guide topic coverage; the numerical economies and questions are original and are not empirical claims about current institutions.",
